  "question": {
    "text": "At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>363</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>, the vapour pressure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>21</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kPa</mi></math> and that of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>18</mn><mi>kPa</mi></math>. One mole of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;moles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> are mixed. Assuming that this solution is ideal, the vapour pressure of the mixture is___________&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kPa</mi></math>. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo></math>Round of to the Nearest Integer<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>)</mo></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "19",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>21</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kPa</mi><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kPa</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> An Ideal solution is prepared by mixing <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;mole <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> mole <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> According to Raoult&#39;s law</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>21</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kPa</mi></math></p>",
